---
import CeilingLeakLayout from '../../../layouts/CeilingLeakLayout.astro';
---

<CeilingLeakLayout>
    <main class="flex flex-col">
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white py-12 dark:bg-[#101622] sm:py-16 lg:py-20">
            <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
                <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
                    <!-- Text Content -->
                    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
                        <!-- Urgency Badge -->
                        <div class="inline-flex w-fit items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-orange-200 bg-orange-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-orange-700 shadow-sm dark:border-orange-900/50 dark:bg-orange-900/20 dark:text-orange-400">
                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sm">warning</span>
                            Structural Collapse Risk: Immediate Action Required
                        </div>
                        <h1 class="text-4xl font-black leading-tight tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
                            Emergency Ceiling Leak Repair & <span class="text-[#135bec]">Restoration</span>
                        </h1>
                        <p class="text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                            Don't wait for the ceiling to fall. We identify the source, stop the leak, and restore your property structurally and aesthetically.
                        </p>
                        <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
                            <a href="/contact/" class="flex h-12 items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded bg-[#135bec] px-6 text-base font-bold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-500/25 transition-transform hover:scale-[1.02] active:scale-[0.98]">
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined">timer</span>
                                Stop the Leak Now (60-Min Response)
                            </a>
                            <a href="/contact/" class="flex h-12 items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded bg-slate-100 px-6 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 transition-colors hover:bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white dark:hover:bg-slate-700">
                                Get a Free Quote
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Trust Signals -->
                        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6 border-t border-slate-100 pt-6 dark:border-slate-800">
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-green-500">verified</span>
                                Restoration Experts
                            </div>
                            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-green-500">verified</span>
                                24/7 Availability
                            </div>
                            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-green-500">verified</span>
                                Insurance Approved
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Hero Image -->
                    <div class="relative">
                        <div class="aspect-[4/3] w-full overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-slate-200 shadow-2xl dark:bg-slate-800">
                            <div class="h-full w-full bg-cover bg-center" data-alt="Severely water damaged ceiling with peeling paint and brown stains" style="background-image: url('https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuBIpYp3k0vjBnJYCkmaPOi2cfpdGCY7tPxPNfThqf5e3_RbyuYqqGFuHy6f-EKkdJMTfgK4B0FDyCgg2__3eotVObq57x3FS1esjX8o24Xf1FdfQdJ7LjOnFESRsV219PLISMm5ALanZANweUffVuKpNHuZO_D90BDS3-XjGXl0fQ98FPjsUnC9H1EhFvbFEozcsjQRB4neY2T_D3BVxzeFN57uvNUg_AhZH5j4Wf0r_OTKaYBVqjfi5fcjEDfveUIrlGKFFiOxkEea');"></div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Floating Badge on Image -->
                        <div class="absolute -bottom-6 -left-6 hidden rounded-lg bg-white p-4 shadow-xl dark:bg-slate-800 md:block">
                            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                                <div class="flex size-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-green-100 text-green-600 dark:bg-green-900/30 dark:text-green-400">
                                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined">security</span>
                                </div>
                                <div>
                                    <p class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Trusted Experts</p>
                                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">100% Satisfaction Guarantee</p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Symptom Checker Bento Grid -->
        <section class="bg-[#f6f6f8] py-16 dark:bg-[#101622]">
            <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
                <div class="mb-10 max-w-2xl">
                    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-4xl">Identify Your Ceiling Damage</h2>
                    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Compare your damage to these common symptoms. Visual identification helps us prepare the right equipment before we arrive.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
                    <!-- Card 1 -->
                    <div class="group relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-white shadow-sm transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md dark:bg-slate-800">
                        <div class="aspect-square w-full overflow-hidden bg-slate-200">
                            <div class="h-full w-full bg-cover bg-center transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-110" data-alt="Ceiling with large brown concentric water rings" style="background-image: url('https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuAh-sU0EXW-gjLBjcLOd0RVJt82CIJfg14c5UiQ4AfyrTduS3BxpN9oH1rsx1nt1f6-5QA_S1egKVQVfMPXOO9aYwOp87-sVQbNMvubi56q4boI-dkxmKeGfNKKQYNNMiSduzA3MaJbSVP4c8WJCJc0EeYSST-8fhYCDN7tHacf3db-ngJQzccvmRjy86Wn7AzddTwJbJ5Ets6qtKiMzWd3Qh-TgWbYepe81N2RhbwV7YTSWy9wwh2IfDYdEb7C-KDmBmFc-6IT2XJN');"></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col p-5">
                            <div class="mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-orange-500">water_drop</span>
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Brown Rings</h3>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Indicates an old or slow leak soaking through drywall layers. The stain is often larger than the visible spot.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Card 2 -->
                    <div class="group relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-white shadow-sm transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md dark:bg-slate-800">
                        <div class="aspect-square w-full overflow-hidden bg-slate-200">
                            <div class="h-full w-full bg-cover bg-center transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-110" data-alt="Drywall ceiling sagging downwards from water weight" style="background-image: url('https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuC8Pae11UAFN9VsNECCxpuLIMJyQiV6aV9X38Af9vsNT-fTWFxfxhIE9ILrScsW4TGeE2nql_2Rzc9wLFQyMc5csqrof-m315nh1NHX543j6mKOejAXTXXxcHQdY0L2KW7jcwff0s31yQC_EdbL8Ye1T30VYupL8k8-kRv7k0V7-1hRN4r-o3Hx-BMwvUUGsxoyY_59-9XJtlbVpFtnmO3QtPxk9FM5GbJy51lVuItdTOL_R6CbdNCFtEOu6Xt6J7VTjvRWgXiKlhII');"></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col p-5">
                            <div class="mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-red-600">warning</span>
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Sagging Drywall</h3>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400"><strong>Urgent:</strong> Water is pooling above. The weight load creates a severe risk of ceiling collapse.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Card 3 -->
                    <div class="group relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-white shadow-sm transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md dark:bg-slate-800">
                        <div class="aspect-square w-full overflow-hidden bg-slate-200">
                            <div class="h-full w-full bg-cover bg-center transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-110" data-alt="Paint bubbling and peeling off a wall surface" style="background-image: url('https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuCJPQliCtARqn_JW6VznGWj241WM6FtCjRAhegkjVZPCfvzl8YpKaYNuGGeWauLQjri6ZVq4Oy6jX9RAu8hBBD7i9AHiIgPGEvuNZc74L1GMqwjiGasuAB7QI3bTHpdntHreMLG_FwCyitcrGF4MZ7wtWlmwMmUPCSis0gSCGMVTC4d6boh14ULw-LGiZZ7AUDLyBj2n-Affpj9a_GSZmC0KA7Wg3i5xmkeaQyuO2f4qgiy249I_17vLO1kqIi8Np8wim3oq70H209C');"></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col p-5">
                            <div class="mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-orange-500">bubble_chart</span>
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Bubbling Paint</h3>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Trapped moisture behind latex paint layers. "Water blisters" should be drained professionally.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Card 4 -->
                    <div class="group relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-white shadow-sm transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-md dark:bg-slate-800">
                        <div class="aspect-square w-full overflow-hidden bg-slate-200">
                            <div class="h-full w-full bg-cover bg-center transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-110" data-alt="Dark mold spots growing in the corner of a ceiling" style="background-image: url('https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuDMWhWrRwaUPS29nVHadUrkRL4jVwKVi0jeOaMM4OIGJR26gSq1InuBsya5bW--PvtrVPm35T1lcy4IwpJzzfbpKeA1iZtwppfHS9w7QzD87XLEGBxyD03Cs0Ifc3lIp7eQXAid3HTNG24Bx1XTb2JLztbipnBx_l_QWRaHwdWKO8kSIDwT5Q03TCDtT52tORS3r_5hGHzoAgmvxFv6PjNUchvt5APxV8GoT8_kEG8cig8j2Lv3W0QGNgMSv4FtYIavLrPWPcBDQvPI');"></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col p-5">
                            <div class="mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-purple-500">coronavirus</span>
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Mold Corners</h3>
                            </div>
                            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Signifies long-standing moisture issues. Requires safe remediation to prevent spore spread.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Technical Process Section -->
        <section class="bg-white py-16 dark:bg-slate-900">
            <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
                <div class="mb-12 text-center">
                    <span class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#135bec] dark:text-[#135bec]">Our Process</span>
                    <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-4xl">We Fix the Source, Not Just the Stain</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-4">
                    <!-- Step 1 -->
                    <div class="relative flex flex-col items-center text-center">
                        <div class="mb-4 flex size-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-50 text-3xl font-bold text-[#135bec] dark:bg-blue-900/20 dark:text-blue-400">1</div>
                        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Source ID</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">We use thermal imaging cameras to locate the exact source of the leak without unnecessary demolition.</p>
                        <!-- Connector Line -->
                        <div class="hidden md:block absolute top-8 left-[60%] w-[80%] border-t-2 border-dashed border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700"></div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Step 2 -->
                    <div class="relative flex flex-col items-center text-center">
                        <div class="mb-4 flex size-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-50 text-3xl font-bold text-[#135bec] dark:bg-blue-900/20 dark:text-blue-400">2</div>
                        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Containment</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">We set up barriers to prevent water or mold from spreading to unaffected areas of your home.</p>
                        <!-- Connector Line -->
                        <div class="hidden md:block absolute top-8 left-[60%] w-[80%] border-t-2 border-dashed border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700"></div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Step 3 -->
                    <div class="relative flex flex-col items-center text-center">
                        <div class="mb-4 flex size-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-50 text-3xl font-bold text-[#135bec] dark:bg-blue-900/20 dark:text-blue-400">3</div>
                        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Structural Drying</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Industrial-grade dehumidifiers and air movers remove moisture from inside the ceiling cavity.</p>
                        <!-- Connector Line -->
                        <div class="hidden md:block absolute top-8 left-[60%] w-[80%] border-t-2 border-dashed border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700"></div>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Step 4 -->
                    <div class="relative flex flex-col items-center text-center">
                        <div class="mb-4 flex size-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-50 text-3xl font-bold text-[#135bec] dark:bg-blue-900/20 dark:text-blue-400">4</div>
                        <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Reconstruction</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">We repair the drywall, texture, and paint, leaving your ceiling looking brand new.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Local Context Section (Florida Causes) -->
        <section class="bg-blue-50 py-16 dark:bg-slate-800/50">
            <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
                <div class="mb-10 flex flex-col justify-between gap-4 md:flex-row md:items-end">
                    <div>
                        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Common Florida Causes</h2>
                        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Understanding why this happens helps prevent future damage.</p>
                    </div>
                    <a href="/resources/" class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-[#135bec] hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-400">
                        View Maintenance Tips <span class="material-symbols-outlined">arrow_forward</span>
                    </a>
                </div>
                <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
                    <div class="flex gap-4 rounded-lg bg-white p-6 shadow-sm dark:bg-slate-900">
                        <div class="shrink-0 rounded bg-blue-100 p-2 text-[#135bec] dark:bg-blue-900/30 dark:text-blue-400 h-fit">
                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined">ac_unit</span>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="mb-1 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">HVAC Condensation</h3>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">In humid climates, clogged condensate lines often overflow into attic pans and leak through ceilings.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex gap-4 rounded-lg bg-white p-6 shadow-sm dark:bg-slate-900">
                        <div class="shrink-0 rounded bg-blue-100 p-2 text-[#135bec] dark:bg-blue-900/30 dark:text-blue-400 h-fit">
                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined">thunderstorm</span>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="mb-1 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Storm Damage</h3>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Roof tiles displaced by high winds allow rainwater to penetrate the underlayment and soak insulation.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex gap-4 rounded-lg bg-white p-6 shadow-sm dark:bg-slate-900">
                        <div class="shrink-0 rounded bg-blue-100 p-2 text-[#135bec] dark:bg-blue-900/30 dark:text-blue-400 h-fit">
                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined">plumbing</span>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="mb-1 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Upstairs Plumbing</h3>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Leaks from bathtubs, toilets, or supply lines on the second floor often manifest as ceiling stains below.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- FAQ Section -->
        <section class="bg-white py-16 dark:bg-[#101622]">
            <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
                <h2 class="mb-8 text-center text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                <div class="space-y-4">
                    <!-- FAQ 1 -->
                    <details class="group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
                        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                            <h3 class="font-bold">Should I pop the water blister in my paint?</h3>
                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">expand_more</span>
                        </summary>
                        <div class="mt-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                            <p><strong>Yes, but act carefully.</strong> Have a bucket ready underneath. Puncturing the blister relieves the weight and prevents the drywall from collapsing. However, this is a temporary fix—you must address the source of the water immediately.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                    <!-- FAQ 2 -->
                    <details class="group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
                        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                            <h3 class="font-bold">Does homeowners insurance cover ceiling leaks?</h3>
                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">expand_more</span>
                        </summary>
                        <div class="mt-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                            <p>Typically, yes. If the damage is "sudden and accidental" (like a burst pipe), most policies cover the restoration. Slow leaks caused by lack of maintenance might not be covered. We can help you navigate the claim process.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                    <!-- FAQ 3 -->
                    <details class="group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
                        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
                            <h3 class="font-bold">How long does the drying process take?</h3>
                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined transition duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">expand_more</span>
                        </summary>
                        <div class="mt-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                            <p>Depending on the extent of the saturation, structural drying usually takes 3 to 5 days. We monitor moisture levels daily to ensure the area is completely dry before starting reconstruction.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
</CeilingLeakLayout>
